    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0169" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Generalissimo
                        Chiang</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d111-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-10">November 10, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and most secret from the President to the Generalissimo</p>
                <p>I am terribly sorry to learn of Madame Chiang’s illness<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d111-f2"/> and sincerely hope that she will be fully recovered in
                    time for our conference.</p>
                <p>I have had a long talk with General Somervell and appreciate very much your
                    courtesies to him. He has given me your private message<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d111-f3"/> as I have already indicated to you.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d111-f4"/></p>
                <p>I agree with you fully that we should meet together before I see Stalin. I want
                    so much to have some good talks with you so, naturally, I am eagerly looking
                    forward to seeing you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
